      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pharmacokinetics and clinical effects of daily oral doses of 100 mg and 200 mg atenolol, respectively, were studied in patients with angina pectoris by means of a double-blind cross-over randomized study. Half-lives and areas under the curve were of the same magnitude as described earlier for healthy volunteers and hypertensive patients. However, a steady state level was built up during 4-week medication of 100 mg or 200 mg atenolol daily. Intra-patient correlations of plasma levels and reductions in exercising heart rate were moderate (r = 0.56-0.85). Only plasma levels and exercising heart rates revealed significant differences after a 100 mg and 200 mg dose. These findings, together with the remaining clinical observations, demonstrated that a single daily dose of 100 mg atenolol is useful in patients with exercise-induced angina pectoris."},
